EXPERIMENT - 2 (LEETCODE Problem 35)


Aim - Given a sorted array of distinct integers and a target value, return the index if the target is found. If not, return the index where it would be if it were inserted in order.

Algortihm - Search Insert Position (Binary Search)

             1. Initialize:
                low = 0
                high = n - 1

             2. Repeat while low <= high:
               a. mid = low + (high - low) / 2
               b. If nums[mid] == target:
                 return mid
               c. Else if nums[mid] < target:
                 low = mid + 1
               d. Else:
                 high = mid - 1

             3. If the target is not found:
                 return low

Code - 

            class Solution {
            public:
            int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {

            int low = 0;
            int high = nums.size() -1 ;

            while (low <= high){
            int mid = low + (high-low) / 2;
  
            if (nums[mid]== target)
            return mid;
            else if (nums[mid]<=target)
            low = mid + 1;
            else
            high = mid - 1;
            }
              return low;
            }
           };
